  "note": "Election of the Limavady Urban District Council, polled Wednesday 20 May 1964; twelve candidates for nine seats (Belfast News-Letter, 21 May 1964, p. 7). The Unionist Party failed in its bid to win all nine seats and lost a seat to the Independents, who now had three members; the printed labels give three Independents (M'Causland, M'Laughlin and Morrison). The name H. W. Hall is printed thus, although the same member appears as H. W. Hull in earlier years."
